unit	"Foundations"
title	"Your first greetings"
description	"Greet someone, ask how they are and respond simply."
teacher_intro	"Let's make your first exchange. You already know that Vietnamese syllables carry tones. Now use a complete phrase. Say the Vietnamese aloud before you reveal it."
background	"Xin chào is a polite greeting. Xin can function as a polite/requesting element, while chào means to greet or say hello. In ordinary conversation, the greeting is often followed by an address term or a question."
culture	"Vietnamese greetings are relationship-sensitive. People often use anh, chị, em, cô, chú or another kinship-style term instead of a neutral 'you'. Bạn is useful for learners but is not suitable for every age or relationship."
