unit	"Foundations"
title	"Introducing yourself"
description	"Say your name, ask another person's name and introduce someone."
teacher_intro	"You can now greet someone. The next step is to tell them your name. We will build the sentence from the small pieces tên, tôi and là. Pause after each English prompt and construct the Vietnamese yourself."
background	"Tên means 'name'. Là is a linking word used in identification and classification. Vietnamese often omits a linking verb in other sentence types, so do not assume là is needed every time English uses 'am' or 'is'."
culture	"Vietnamese names commonly include a family name, optional middle name and given name. The given name is often the final element. When addressing someone, people usually use the appropriate given name with a relationship term rather than the full name alone."
dialogue	
0	
speaker	"TEACHER · ENGLISH"
line	"First say 'name': tên. Now say 'my': tôi. Put them together: tên tôi — my name."
1	
speaker	"STUDENT 1"
line	"Tên tôi."
2	
speaker	"TEACHER · ENGLISH"
line	"Now add là, the linking word: tên tôi là… — my name is… Put your own name at the end."
3	
speaker	"STUDENT 2"
line	"Tên tôi là Anna."
4	
speaker	"TEACHER · ENGLISH"
