unit	"Foundations"
title	"Where are you from?"
description	"Say your nationality, country of origin and where you live."
teacher_intro	"Now combine what you know: tôi, là and a new word người. Then learn how to say where you come from and where you live. Build each phrase in stages."
background	"Người means 'person' or 'people'. In người Việt, it means a Vietnamese person; in người Úc, an Australian person. Đến từ means 'come from', while sống ở means 'live in/at'."
culture	"Country and nationality labels do not always map one-to-one onto English categories. In conversation, speakers may ask quê ở đâu? ('Where is your home place/from?') as well as asking which country someone comes from."
