unit	"Foundations"
title	"Polite words"
description	"Use thanks, apologies, excuse me and simple requests."
teacher_intro	"Politeness in Vietnamese is not only a list of magic words. It also comes from choosing the right way to address someone. First learn a few useful expressions, then notice how they fit into a relationship."
background	"Cảm ơn means 'thank you'. Xin lỗi is used for 'sorry' and can also get someone's attention politely. Làm ơn is a request expression similar to 'please'."
culture	"A phrase can be grammatically correct but still sound distant or overly formal if the pronouns do not fit. Listen to how Vietnamese speakers address one another, and learn the relationship terms alongside the phrases."
