unit	"Foundations"
title	"Numbers 0–20"
description	"Count from zero to twenty and use numbers in simple questions."
teacher_intro	"Numbers are building blocks you will use every day. Learn the basic sequence, then use it in a question. Say each number aloud; pay special attention to the tones."
background	"The basic numbers are không, một, hai, ba, bốn, năm, sáu, bảy, tám, chín, mười. From eleven to nineteen, the pattern is mười + number. Twenty is hai mươi."
culture	"Vietnamese number forms can change slightly in compounds: for example, five is năm, but in some number combinations it is pronounced/lowered to lăm, as in mười lăm (15). This is a regular spoken pattern."
dialogue	
0	
speaker	"TEACHER · ENGLISH"
