unit	"Foundations"
title	"Age and basic details"
description	"Ask and answer age and give a simple personal detail."
teacher_intro	"Now use numbers to talk about age. Vietnamese expresses age without a separate word for 'am' in this pattern. Build the question first, then answer it."
background	"Tuổi means age or years of age. Bao nhiêu means how many/how much. The pattern bạn bao nhiêu tuổi? is a straightforward learner question."
culture	"Age can help Vietnamese speakers choose suitable pronouns and forms of address. In some situations asking age early is practical rather than intrusive, because it helps establish whether to use anh, chị, em, cô, chú and so on."
